00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.210
How many soldiers you have?

00:16:59.430 --> 00:16:59.970
Oh, soldiers.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:15.810
Soldiers, Ken, Ken, me, of course, you know, Speed, Tucker, not many, Jose, not many.

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:19.600
Well, the authorities are clamping down on me recruiting campaign, you know, what can

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:20.100
you do, right?

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:22.140
Maybe you should hire mercenaries.

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:23.960
Yes?

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:24.640
Mercenaries?

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:29.770
Si, and then when my victory is complete, I will send you troops, one thousand.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:35.360
brave young men with lion hearts, guns, munitions. Together, Wolfie, we will take tooting in a

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:48.280
wave of fire. But first, I must comb my hair. Bloody potty. Look, Wolfie, if you go taking

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:53.020
tooting in a wave of fire, mark my words, you'll go straight back on probation. Look, if I

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:59.780
want to take tooting, I'll do it on me own, all right? I need his help. Just his money.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:05.890
Okay? Troops. What's he on about? Can you imagine a thousand Spaniards marching through

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:15.100
Tooting Broadway? He did look like a lightning strike at a wimpy bar. What sort of mercenaries

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:22.250
am I gonna get on £16.50 a week doll money? A Chelsea pensioner's and a beef eater after

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:27.320
some pin money? Better than nothing. Yeah, but they're hardly dogs of war, are they,

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:29.960
Ken? You know what I mean? I mean, I couldn't see them putting a-

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:37.750
frights up the SAS. I mean, the way he talks. You'd think revolution was simple. Well, I've

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:46.690
heard you talk like him before now. Yeah, but he's sober. No, I mean, look, I want a revolution,

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:51.740
Ken. I mean, let's get this straight, you know, but a sort of gentle revolution. Right. You know?

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:58.990
Yeah. I mean, what's the popular front ever done that's really subversive, eh? Hey, threw a brick

00:18:58.990 --> 00:18:59.810
at a town hall once.

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:00.590
And missed?

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:00.970
Exactly.

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:04.170
I know Jose's got a violent streak.

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:06.220
He wouldn't have thrown a brick at the town hall.

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:07.700
He'd have blown the bloody thing up.

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:11.670
And he has a cheek to read my master plan.

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:14.820
Why don't you ask him to leave?

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:16.890
I will.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.100
As soon as he gives me the money.

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:19.700
Right, come on.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:25.010
Oh, going out, Jose.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:27.690
Si, I've been invited to dine with the Johnsons.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:29.760
Oh, that's a turn-up, innit?

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:32.810
I've been here eight months and never been invited down for a cream cracker.

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.650
You're always eating down here.

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:36.310
I know, but I've never been invited.

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:41.850
I think Senor Johnson wants me to, how you say, meet his daughter, eh?

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:42.290
Eh?

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:43.250
Eh, eh, eh.

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:44.030
Oi.

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:45.210
Oh, hang on, hang on.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:48.900
Shirley and me have got an understanding, right?

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:50.270
I do not know what you mean.

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:55.370
You, look, you're not dealing with a couple of mugs, son.

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:57.750
You know, we're hardened terrorists, you know.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:19:59.980
Ah, no, no, no, no.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:00.760
I think you misunderstand.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:04.220
On my travels, I meet many people in many different countries.

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:05.100
They are friends.

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:06.690
It will be the same with Shirley.

00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:07.730
Only a friend.

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:10.380
Please, I'm sorry.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:11.360
That's all right, yeah?

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:12.400
No, there's no problem.

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:15.680
It is how you say, wham, bam, thank you, ma'am.

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:19.490
I'll kill him.

00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:20.830
Do you remember what he said?

00:20:21.140 --> 00:20:21.920
I'll kill him.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:22.820
I'll break his...

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:23.800
I'll get speed.

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:25.840
Wolfie, he doesn't know what it means.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:27.360
Oh, he knows what it means, all right.

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:28.340
I'll talk to him.

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:35.210
Where's Hosey?

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.230
Mum's showing in the garden.

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:39.120
But it's pitch black.

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:40.320
Try telling her that.

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:42.000
Oh, God almighty.

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:44.920
Sometimes I think that woman's got a mind of her own.

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:50.490
He's a nice lad, isn't he, love?

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:51.880
He's pleasant enough.

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:54.330
He's not taking his eyes off you.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:56.900
He's probably suffering from frostbite, Dad.

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:59.980
If, um, if he should invite...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:07.120
you over to his daddy's estate, you know, for a holiday. Well, I wouldn't mind. You're going to

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:11.540
Spain with Jose, but you screamed the ass down when I went on holiday with Wolfie. Well, there's a bit

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:21.790
of a difference between a chateau in San Sebastian and a tent in Gravesend. Senora Johnson, what is

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:27.340
this? Oh, it's a dog lovey. Look, scrape it off on this stuff.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:35.670
It is a very nice garden, senor.

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:36.870
Oh, thank you.

00:21:37.050 --> 00:21:39.830
Of course, the darkness doesn't do it justice.

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:44.070
You see, my garden is designed as a furry ghetto.

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:45.160
Grotto.

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:46.720
Grotto?

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:47.880
I never hear this word.

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:49.340
You stick with me, son.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:52.490
I will learn you mucho good English.

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:53.300
Gracias.

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:54.480
Por favor.

00:21:55.030 --> 00:21:55.750
Por favor.

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:56.950
Oh, you speak Spanish?

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:58.070
Well, uh...

00:21:58.070 --> 00:21:59.970
He learned that from high chaparral.

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:04.820
More sangria, Jose?

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:07.480
Oh, no, gracias. Maybe you have some hot chocolate, huh?

00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:11.460
Hot chocolate? But I made this sangria specially for you.

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:13.080
There's another gallon and a half in the fridge.

00:22:13.280 --> 00:22:14.700
He's freezing, Dad.

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:17.160
Rubbish! It's bracing.

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:21.970
Anyway, we've all got a nice hot paella in our bellies.

00:22:22.190 --> 00:22:24.570
Oh, sí, the paella was very nice, señora.

00:22:24.870 --> 00:22:26.250
She got it out of a tin, Jose.

00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:29.160
She did not get it out of a tin, Shirley.

00:22:29.420 --> 00:22:29.980
Did you love?

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:34.180
No, not. I've got the packet to prove it.

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:39.500
Well, we'll leave you two youngsters to enjoy the evening.

00:22:39.760 --> 00:22:42.200
Oh, yes. We're going to the wall.

00:22:43.280 --> 00:22:45.790
See you later.

00:23:02.590 --> 00:23:05.470
Do you think our Shirley likes him, love?

00:23:05.850 --> 00:23:07.250
Oh, I don't know, love.

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:10.280
Now, he's the sort of man I wouldn't mind her marrying.

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:13.140
Yes, but Shirley's engaged to Foxy.

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:15.940
Ah, that's because she's never met real class.

00:23:16.610 --> 00:23:20.450
No, I'd rather her marry Spanish nobility than that lefty layabout.

00:23:21.660 --> 00:23:24.900
Come to think of it, I'd rather her marry a Chinese rickshaw driver.

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:29.060
Yeah, shall I let mints out to them?

00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:29.980
You can't.

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:33.560
You can't have chocolate mints on top of paella. Do you want him to be sick?

00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:35.560
Not on our new patio.

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:41.480
Let's leave them alone out there. I don't want nothing to disturb their peace.

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:46.060
Ah, be shoddy about.

00:23:47.100 --> 00:23:47.880
She's not here.

00:23:48.140 --> 00:23:49.690
I see that.

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:50.610
Where is she?

00:23:50.810 --> 00:23:51.730
None of your business.

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:54.070
Did your team win, Foxy?

00:23:54.190 --> 00:23:55.530
No, Mrs. J, they lost.

00:23:55.870 --> 00:23:56.050
Ah.

00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:57.690
Not his day, is it?

00:23:57.890 --> 00:23:58.010
Yeah.

00:23:58.330 --> 00:23:58.570
Oi!

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:02.510
What do you think you're playing at?

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:04.160
Nothing, love, nothing.

00:24:04.320 --> 00:24:08.040
You're doing your Cupid impersonation, leaving me and Jose out on the patio like that.

00:24:08.310 --> 00:24:10.230
I just thought you'd have a lot to talk about.

00:24:10.410 --> 00:24:12.130
We haven't got anything to talk about.

00:24:12.230 --> 00:24:14.470
I've sat out there all evening in a Gale Falls night.

00:24:14.530 --> 00:24:17.710
I've got frostbite on me fingers, and I've listened to every Spanish record,

00:24:17.870 --> 00:24:20.670
from Donkey Serenade to Tommy Steele's Little White Ball.

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:24.060
I just wanted you to enjoy yourself, love.

00:24:24.160 --> 00:24:26.860
Dad, when are you going to understand that I don't enjoy myself?

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:28.460
I just want to be with Wolfie.

00:24:38.160 --> 00:24:39.380
Where's, uh, where's house signing?

00:24:39.700 --> 00:24:40.660
On the patio.

00:24:50.820 --> 00:24:53.160
Spanish royalty call their in-laws.

00:24:53.770 --> 00:24:54.830
I don't know.

00:24:55.290 --> 00:24:56.810
Mum and Dad, I suppose.

00:24:57.130 --> 00:24:58.310
Oh, bloody Nora.

00:25:03.200 --> 00:25:03.800
Hello, citizen.

00:25:04.200 --> 00:25:05.690
Oh, here.

00:25:06.700 --> 00:25:07.100
Here.

00:25:07.300 --> 00:25:08.720
You've got an ice cube in your eye.

00:25:09.150 --> 00:25:09.510
Si.

00:25:09.850 --> 00:25:11.470
It is an old Spanish custom.

00:25:11.850 --> 00:25:15.070
When you have eaten in a restaurant, before you pay the bill, you...

00:25:15.070 --> 00:25:16.510
Stick ice cubes in your eye.

00:25:16.590 --> 00:25:16.810
Si.

00:25:16.990 --> 00:25:17.710
Sure, sure.

00:25:18.640 --> 00:25:20.760
Yeah, we've got an old English custom, you know.

00:25:21.400 --> 00:25:25.440
When we eat in a restaurant, before we pay the bill, we make a run for it.

00:25:26.570 --> 00:25:27.530
This is permitted?

00:25:28.010 --> 00:25:29.490
If you're close to the door, it is, yeah.

00:25:31.050 --> 00:25:33.500
Yeah, I'm glad we're on our own.

00:25:33.780 --> 00:25:36.030
I say, I want to talk business.

00:25:36.700 --> 00:25:37.100
Business?

00:25:37.500 --> 00:25:40.540
Oh, you know, revolutionary business, financial support.

00:25:41.630 --> 00:25:41.850
Si.

00:25:42.770 --> 00:25:44.860
Right, how much?

00:25:45.650 --> 00:25:47.310
Well, how much can you afford to give us?

00:25:47.390 --> 00:25:49.150
Well, I was thinking in terms of...

00:25:50.100 --> 00:25:50.680
What?

00:25:51.780 --> 00:25:52.520
What did you say?

00:25:52.760 --> 00:25:54.720
I said, how much can you afford to give us?

00:25:55.400 --> 00:25:56.200
What do you mean, give you?

00:25:56.680 --> 00:25:57.660
No, we're Brassic.

00:25:58.330 --> 00:25:58.730
Brassic?

00:25:58.970 --> 00:25:59.710
Brassic lint.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:06.460
you know, niche, the coin, nothing, nil. You have no money? Look, we are somewhat had by the

00:26:06.460 --> 00:26:12.820
financial curlies, you know what I mean? You said you'd come to give us money. But you sent us a letter

00:26:12.820 --> 00:26:19.960
offering your support. Yeah, yeah, yeah, support, not money. Oh, look, you must have bread, you're a

00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:26.600
duke, son. Oh, see, my father, he is very rich, but he gives nothing to me. Huh? He has disowned me,

00:26:26.840 --> 00:26:29.960
take my name from his will. Well, all right, well, look, just...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.440
Can't you go back to Bilbao and have a whip round for me?

00:26:32.680 --> 00:26:36.680
Listen, Wolfie, my comrades have to hold a collection to buy my aeroplane ticket.

00:26:36.880 --> 00:26:38.260
And there are only seven of us.

00:26:38.400 --> 00:26:41.020
Well, eh? Seven?

00:26:41.220 --> 00:26:41.400
Si.

00:26:42.580 --> 00:26:44.660
What about 1,000 young warriors?

00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:46.160
They're in your think tank.

00:26:46.970 --> 00:26:47.830
Oh, my God.

00:26:48.890 --> 00:26:50.750
It's like the militant faction of a sooty club.

00:26:51.190 --> 00:26:51.810
Sooty club?

00:26:52.110 --> 00:26:53.570
You've got a right nerve, though, sir.

00:26:53.690 --> 00:26:56.390
You come here with your Latin charm, your wide-awake whistle,

00:26:56.610 --> 00:26:59.230
even have the audacity to read my secret master plan.

00:26:59.410 --> 00:26:59.970
And you, you...

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:03.660
send me a letter with no stamp on it. Look, citizen, amongst the International League

00:27:03.660 --> 00:27:07.900
of Revolutionaries, the no stamp symbol is revered. International League of Revolutionaries,

00:27:08.020 --> 00:27:15.410
ha. What do you mean? Ha. What do you mean, ha? Ha. You know what a Black September call

00:27:15.410 --> 00:27:24.370
me, eh? Man Mountain. Man Mountain? You mean Molchil. Molchil, eh? Si. Right, you deep-rocked

00:27:24.370 --> 00:27:28.360
aristocrat. You know, they should have called you, Osay. They should have called you Harry

00:27:28.360 --> 00:27:29.880
Rontz. Harry, who is this?

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:30.420
Harry Rons.

00:27:30.520 --> 00:27:31.100
Pont, citizen.

00:27:31.380 --> 00:27:31.520
Pont.

00:27:31.640 --> 00:27:32.300
Hey, watch the suit.

00:27:32.980 --> 00:27:34.320
They're arguing, Charles.

00:27:34.640 --> 00:27:36.100
I don't care, Florence.

00:27:36.260 --> 00:27:38.120
Let them beat each other to a pulp.

00:27:38.800 --> 00:27:40.800
Is that Yeti interfering with everything?

00:27:41.370 --> 00:27:44.250
Shirley putting her own personal feelings before a title.

00:27:45.070 --> 00:27:46.730
And that paella's coming back on me.

00:27:46.830 --> 00:27:47.490
I'm fed up.

00:27:47.730 --> 00:27:48.190
I am.

00:27:48.310 --> 00:27:49.170
I'm fed up, Florence.

00:27:49.370 --> 00:27:49.530
Hey!

00:27:50.840 --> 00:27:52.500
What are you doing with my ice cube?

00:27:52.820 --> 00:27:54.740
Oh, it's just an old Spanish custom.

00:27:55.560 --> 00:27:56.360
Oh, bleedin' lay.
